{"id":"h4-06-e1","title":"Delivery semantics and idempotency","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: at-most/at-least/exactly-once myths and dedup keys. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"why-delivery-is-never-perfect","title":"Why delivery is never perfect","html":"<p><strong>Networks lose packets and acknowledgements, and processes crash between \"did the work\" and \"told anyone\".</strong> So a sender can never be sure whether a message arrived. This is the Two Generals problem: you can't have certainty with an unreliable channel.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 552 68\" width=\"552\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The ack can be lost even if the work succeeded\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 34 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 34 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M394 34 L450 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M394 34 L450 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Producer</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Broker</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"349\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Consumer</text><rect x=\"450\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"495\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Database</text></svg><figcaption>The ack can be lost even if the work succeeded</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Consider the consumer crash windows: (A) crash before doing the work, (B) crash after the work but before the ack/commit. In (B) the broker will redeliver, and the work is done twice.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Payment consumer debits 500 rupees, then crashes before committing the offset. On restart it reads the same message and debits again: 1,000 charged. This is real; it is why every payment system obsesses over idempotency.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Stripe, Razorpay, PayU and UPI rails all publish rules for duplicate protection (idempotency keys, transaction reference IDs) because retries are expected.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> You post a letter and do not hear back. Resend it and risk two copies, or do not and risk none.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Claiming a design \"never duplicates\".</li>\n<li>Not identifying where exactly the crash windows are.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"at-most-once-at-least-once-exactly-once","title":"At-most-once, at-least-once, exactly-once","html":"<p><strong>Three delivery guarantees:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>At-most-once:</strong> send, never retry. Can lose messages, never duplicates. Commit offset first, then process. Fine for metrics, logs, GPS pings.</li>\n<li><strong>At-least-once:</strong> retry until acknowledged. Never loses, may duplicate. Process first, then commit. The default for most real systems.</li>\n<li><strong>Exactly-once:</strong> each message's effect happens once. Not achievable as pure <em>delivery</em> over an unreliable network; achievable as <em>effect</em> by combining at-least-once with idempotent or transactional processing.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 552 68\" width=\"552\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"At-least-once: process, then ack\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 34 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 34 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M394 34 L450 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M394 34 L450 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Broker</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Consumer</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"349\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Process</text><rect x=\"450\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"495\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Ack</text></svg><figcaption>At-least-once: process, then ack</figcaption></figure>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Guarantee</th>\n<th>Loses data</th>\n<th>Duplicates</th>\n<th>Cost</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>At-most-once</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>Cheapest</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>At-least-once</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>Needs dedup</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Exactly-once effect</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>No (effect)</td>\n<td>Extra state, latency</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Gravity.</strong> Default to at-least-once plus idempotent consumers. It is the most robust approach and easy to reason about. Reverting later is easy since the architecture does not change; adding idempotency afterwards means changing every side effect.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Likes counter: duplicates inflate by 0.01%: acceptable with at-most/at-least. Bank transfer: not acceptable; needs an effect-once design.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Kafka's default producer/consumer pattern is at-least-once; SQS Standard is at-least-once; MQTT defines QoS 0, 1 and 2 matching these three.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Delivery with a tracking signature: a courier who retries until signed may deliver twice.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Mixing up commit-before and commit-after processing.</li>\n<li>Treating \"exactly-once\" as a free setting.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"the-exactly-once-myth-and-kafka-s-version","title":"The exactly-once myth and Kafka's version","html":"<p><strong>\"Exactly-once delivery\" is a marketing phrase. What systems really give is exactly-once <em>processing effects</em> within a controlled boundary.</strong></p>\n<p>Kafka offers, within Kafka only:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Idempotent producer</strong> (<code>enable.idempotence=true</code>, default in modern clients): each producer gets a producer ID and per-partition sequence numbers; the broker drops duplicates from retries. Removes duplicates and reordering from producer retries.</li>\n<li><strong>Transactions</strong> (<code>transactional.id</code>): atomically write to several partitions and commit consumer offsets together; readers use <code>isolation.level=read_committed</code>. This enables consume-process-produce pipelines (Kafka Streams <code>processing.guarantee=exactly_once_v2</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The guarantee ends at Kafka's edge. If your processor also calls a payment API or writes to MySQL, those side effects are outside the transaction and can still be repeated; there you need idempotency keys or a transactional outbox/inbox.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 454 130\" width=\"454\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Kafka transactions cover read-process-write inside Kafka only\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M115.2 65 L171.2 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 65 L171.2 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M261.2 65 L317.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M261.2 65 L317.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M261.2 65 L317.2 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M261.2 65 L317.2 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"63.6\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Input topic</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"216.2\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Processor</text><rect x=\"317.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"379.59999999999997\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Output topic</text><rect x=\"317.2\" y=\"74\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"379.59999999999997\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Offsets commit</text></svg><figcaption>Kafka transactions cover read-process-write inside Kafka only</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Stream job reads <code>orders</code>, writes <code>order_totals</code>. With EOS v2, a crash mid-way aborts the transaction; the output messages written are invisible to read_committed consumers and the input offset is not advanced, so the retry produces the totals once. But if the job also POSTs to an email provider, an email can go twice.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Confluent popularised this in Kafka 0.11 (2017). Flink offers exactly-once via checkpoints plus two-phase commit sinks.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Trading cards only counted once if you stamp them in the same room that holds the album; outside that room, stamps are not tracked.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Saying \"Kafka gives exactly-once, done\" when the sink is an external system.</li>\n<li>Forgetting <code>read_committed</code> on consumers; otherwise aborted data is visible.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"idempotency-and-dedup-keys","title":"Idempotency and dedup keys","html":"<p><strong>An operation is idempotent if doing it twice gives the same result as doing it once.</strong> <code>SET balance=500</code> is idempotent; <code>balance = balance - 100</code> is not. The practical technique: give every logical operation a unique <strong>idempotency key</strong> and remember which keys you have already processed.</p>\n<p>Design:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Client generates a key (UUID) per intended action and reuses it on retry (Stripe <code>Idempotency-Key</code> header).</li>\n<li>Server stores <code>key -> result</code> in a table with a <strong>unique constraint</strong>, in the same transaction as the side effect.</li>\n<li>On a repeat key, return the stored result without redoing work.</li>\n<li>Expire keys after a window (Stripe keeps them about 24 hours).</li>\n</ol>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">CREATE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> TABLE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> processed_messages</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  msg_id   </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">TEXT</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> PRIMARY KEY</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  result   JSONB,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  created_at </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">TIMESTAMPTZ</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> DEFAULT</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> now</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">()</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">BEGIN</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">INSERT INTO</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> processed_messages(msg_id) </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">VALUES</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">'evt_123'</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">);  </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">-- fails on duplicate</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">UPDATE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> accounts </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">SET</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> balance </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> balance </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">-</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 500</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> WHERE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> id </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 7</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">COMMIT</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">;</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 565.2 68\" width=\"565.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The unique key makes retries harmless\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 34 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 34 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M407.2 34 L463.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M407.2 34 L463.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Client</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">API</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"355.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Dedup table</text><rect x=\"463.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"508.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Accounts</text></svg><figcaption>The unique key makes retries harmless</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Other tricks: natural keys (order ID plus event type), conditional writes (<code>UPDATE ... WHERE version = 3</code>), upserts, and using the Kafka coordinates <code>(topic, partition, offset)</code> as a dedup key.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> A consumer sees <code>payment-captured</code> for order 42 twice. First: inserts key <code>(42, captured)</code> and updates the order. Second: insert hits the unique constraint; code treats it as \"already done\" and acks. Table growth: 10M messages/day x 50 bytes = 500 MB/day, so TTL-clean after 7 days (3.5 GB).</p>\n<p><strong>Gravity.</strong> The dedup record and the side effect must commit <strong>atomically</strong>, otherwise the crash window returns. In a different store (Redis <code>SETNX</code> then DB write), you again have a window. Prefer same-database dedup.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Stripe idempotency keys; AWS SQS FIFO <code>MessageDeduplicationId</code> (5 min window); Razorpay and UPI use reference IDs; Kafka idempotent producers.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A cinema ticket with a number: scanning the same ticket twice at the gate does not let two people in.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Checking \"have I seen this?\" with a read, then writing later (race). Use a unique constraint.</li>\n<li>Generating a new key on each client retry, which defeats the purpose.</li>\n<li>Dedup window shorter than the maximum redelivery delay.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"putting-it-together-a-safe-consumer","title":"Putting it together: a safe consumer","html":"<p><strong>Recipe for a reliable consumer:</strong> at-least-once delivery, idempotent handler, commit after success, retries with backoff, DLQ for poison messages.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">void</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> onMessage</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(ConsumerRecord</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">String, Event</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">></span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> r) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">  try</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">var</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> tx </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> db.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">begin</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">()) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    if</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">!</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">tx.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">insertIfAbsent</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"processed\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, r.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">value</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">().</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">id</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">())) { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">ack</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(r); </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">return</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">; } </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// duplicate</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">    applyBusinessLogic</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(r.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">value</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(), tx);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    tx.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">commit</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  } </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">catch</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (TransientException </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">e</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">) { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">throw</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> e; }   </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// retry later</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">  catch</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (PermanentException </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">e</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">) { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">sendToDlq</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(r, e); }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">  ack</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(r);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">}</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 746 68\" width=\"746\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Safe path: dedup + business write in one transaction\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;0.201;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M261.2 34 L317.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M261.2 34 L317.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;0.401;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M442 34 L498 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M442 34 L498 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M588 34 L644 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M588 34 L644 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Message</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"209.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Dedup check</text><rect x=\"317.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"379.59999999999997\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Business write</text><rect x=\"498\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"543\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Commit</text><rect x=\"644\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"689\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Ack</text></svg><figcaption>Safe path: dedup + business write in one transaction</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> 1,000 msgs/s, 0.1% duplicates = 1 duplicate/s: dedup insert adds about 1 ms per message. The unique index lookup is cheap relative to the cost of a double charge.</p>\n<p><strong>Gravity.</strong> This pattern is reversible and cheap to adopt per service; skipping it is the expensive choice when the first incident arrives.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Payment processors, ledger services and order systems (Shopify, Uber) all follow \"at-least-once plus idempotent writes\".</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A bank teller who checks the cheque number against the \"already cashed\" ledger before paying.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Acking before the DB commit (data loss).</li>\n<li>Not distinguishing transient from permanent errors.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>Crash windows between work and ack make duplicates unavoidable; plan for them.</li>\n<li>At-most-once may lose, at-least-once may duplicate; exactly-once is an effect achieved by dedup or transactions.</li>\n<li>Kafka EOS (idempotent producer, transactions, <code>read_committed</code>) works only inside Kafka; external side effects need their own idempotency.</li>\n<li>Idempotency key plus a unique constraint, committed atomically with the side effect, is the core technique.</li>\n<li>Default recipe: at-least-once, idempotent handler, commit after, backoff retry, DLQ.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}